    "state": "{\"description\":\"Anthony's brother and reflow2's second user — uses it for real on his own projects via grok build, and is the source of the consumer-kit feedback. Design contributor: the 2026-07-24 idea list (bulk spec ingest, team-scale conflicts, rubber-ducking, inherited-project onboarding) came from a conversation between the two of them, and recovering intent from test results is his. Recorded as a Contributor so authorship attributes to the person whose word it is, rather than defaulting to whoever relayed it. **He is a USER of reflow2, not a developer of it** (Anthony, 2026-08-18) — his reports are field evidence about the product.\\n\\n═══ BACKGROUND, 2026-08-18 ═══\\n**Software applications engineer. Bachelor's degree in BIOLOGY.**\\n\\n⚠️ **RELAYED BY ANTHONY, NOT SELF-DESCRIBED.** Alex has not written or confirmed this himself. `dec:idea-a-user-carries-a-persona-that-shapes-every-reply` records that self-described and assigned are not the same thing, and that the difference is probably what separates a good feature from a stereotype — so this stands as a starting point to be corrected by him, never as a settled reading of the man.\\n\\n⭐ THE TWO HALVES DIVERGE, AND THAT IS THE USEFUL PART. He writes application software but trained in life sciences, so living-systems framing, taxonomy and classification are likely native ground — and the deep-computer-science framings a career software engineer would take for granted are the ones worth unpacking rather than assuming. **Offered as a lead for how to pitch an explanation, not as a claim about what he knows.**\\n\\n📌 WHAT HE IS ACTUALLY DOING WITH REFLOW2, and it shapes what he needs: building the knowledge base for a LARGE project at work, roughly 20% of the inputs entered as of 2026-08-18, and about to show it to coworkers who have never seen reflow2. Two live consequences, both open: `dec:idea-a-project-says-what-it-is-doing-now-so-the-loop-stops-pushing` (the loop presses him to close while he is still capturing) and `dec:idea-the-enum-question-came-back-four-days-after-it-was-fixed`.\",\"handle\":\"@bro\",\"kind\":\"person\",\"name\":\"Alex\"}",
